arning, time, materials and risks before any destructive or exposure-producing trial. No tasting or ingestion.\\\",\\\"effects\\\":\\\"If feasible, enable a bounded practical assessment with recorded method, evidence, uncertainty and scope. If no valid non-ingestive method is available, report that limitation and unmet prerequisites rather than declaring the root safe.\\\"}},\\\"repeat\\\":1,\\\"until\\\":null,\\\"guard\\\":null}],\\\"repeat\\\":1,\\\"until\\\":null,\\\"interrupts\\\":[],\\\"notes\\\":[\\\"Root appearance and another person's meal do not establish absence of toxicity.\\\",\\\"The requested method is not yet an available or mastered capability; its response determines the next practical step.\\\"],\\\"preferences\\\":[\\\"Preserve safe portable food and freedom of movement.\\\",\\\"Avoid unsupported construction or food-safety claims.\\\"],\\\"projects\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"portable-provisions\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"active\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"Can I maintain safe portable provisions and test a useful longer-term storage method?\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"At tick 37 I carry eight berries in two stacks; health is 100, satiety 86.7 and energy 39.4.\\\",\\\"Known berry nutrition is 8 per unit with toxicity zero.\\\",\\\"Root inspection established a whole food item, but visual traits were unavailable in darkness and food safety was not established.\\\",\\\"I observed Moss consume two roots; this is evidence of consumption, not a toxicity assessment.\\\"],\\\"uncertainty\\\":\\\"Root safety and preparation remain unknown. Rack materials and practical storage performance remain untested.\\\",\\\"goal\\\":\\\"Maintain safe provisions and freedom of movement while investigating storage without assuming a benefit.\\\",\\\"completedSteps\\\":[\\\"Collected and ate known-safe berries.\\\",\\\"Replenished carried berries.\\\",\\\"Mastered ventilated food storage.\\\",\\\"Observed and qualitatively inspected the nearby root source.\\\"],\\\"outputs\\\":[\\\"Eig